fix(isolation): per-account engine arbiter + OAuth callback fix

- Engine arbiter is now keyed by account session id instead of a global
  singleton: each connected Deriv account runs its autonomous engine,
  bots and journal fully independently, even in the same browser/laptop.
- All engines (speed-ai, bot, dual-lock, killshot, killshot-family,
  twin-hedge) register ownership under the account session, so enabling
  autonomous trading in one account can never disable another's.
- healthz reports per-ownership state; connect page surfaces OAuth
  callback errors.
